#==============================================================================================
#
#   cubics - chopping a monotonic cubic where it crosses a clip line
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Skia m144's double-precision root finders and the code that uses them to chop
#       a cubic exactly at a clip edge: src/base/SkFloatingPoint.cpp (sk_double_nearly_zero,
#       sk_doubles_nearly_equal_ulps), src/base/SkQuads.cpp (Discriminant, Roots, RootsReal),
#       src/base/SkCubics.cpp (RootsReal, RootsValidT, BinarySearchRootsValidT, EvalAt),
#       src/base/SkBezierCurves.cpp (SkBezierCubic::ConvertToPolynomial, Subdivide) and
#       src/core/SkGeometry.cpp (first_axis_intersection, SkChopMonoCubicAtX/Y). tiny-skia
#       ports the older SkPathOps intersection instead, which picks slightly different t values.
#
#       Copyright (c) 2023 Google LLC
